    "history": "Ottoman branch of the Jezreel Valley Railway (the \"Samaria Railway\"), 1050 mm gauge, opened c.1913–1914. Intended to reach Jerusalem via the Hejaz/Haifa–Deraa line but never built beyond Nablus. Closed 1932 for lack of traffic. Mas'udiya was the junction with the British Eastern Railway (to Tulkarm and Lydda, 1918).",
